n:**\n\nI choose **d7-d5** because it's the most principled move that directly contests White's central superiority. It opens my dark-squared bishop on c8, fights for space, and follows classical opening principles of controlling the center with pawns. This move prevents White from consolidating their advantage and gives me counterplay.\n\n**Answer:** P: d7-d5"}
